METHOD
For every half-level K through 30, wall n through 4, reduced factor q,
and row r, the analyzer constructs the exact payment coefficient
sequence eta and its cumulative potential

  E(v)=sum_(t=0)^v eta(t).

It checks coefficientwise E(v)>=0 through five full periods after the
active wall, the period monotonicity E(v+L)>=E(v), and the initial
split inequality

  sum_(v=0)^(x-1)E(v)+sum_(v=0)^(L-x-2)E(v)
    <=sum_(v=0)^(L-1)E(v)

for every 0<=x<L.  All checks are exact signed-integer calculations.
The maximum last nonzero period increment occurs 28 indices after the
active wall, consistent with the exact proof that the potential is
eventually L-periodic.

These zero failures audit Lemma AIMPP; the manuscript proof uses the
explicit stable suffix weights and does not rely on the bounded run.

COMPILER FLAGS
g++ -O2 -std=c++20 -Wall -Wextra -Wpedantic -Wconversion \
  -Wsign-conversion -Wshadow -Werror \
  analyze_su2_aim_period_potential.cpp \
  -o analyze_su2_aim_period_potential

